    </li> <li> <para-num num="[0100]"> </para-num> <div id="p-0100" num="0100" class="description-line"> As described in the Tables 1-4, the present invention is advantageous in that extrusion and stretching processes are easily conducted, and thus, it is possible to stably produce a microporous high density polyethylene film of the present invention and the productivity is improved, and that since the microporous film has the excellent gas permeability, tensile-strength and puncture strength, and low shrinkage, it can be usefully applied to a battery separator and various filters. </div>
    </li> <li> <para-num num="[0101]"> </para-num> <div id="p-0101" num="0101" class="description-line"> The present invention has been described in an illustrative manner, and it is to be understood that the terminology used is intended to be in the nature of description rather than of limitation. Many modifications and variations of the present invention are possible in light of the above teachings. Therefore, it is to be understood that within the scope of the appended claims, the invention may be practiced otherwise than as specifically described. </div>
    
  </li> </ul>
  </div>
  </section>

  <section itemprop="claims" itemscope>
    <h2>Claims (<span itemprop="count">8</span>)</h2>
    
    <div itemprop="content" html><div mxw-id="PCLM7225236" lang="EN" load-source="patent-office" class="claims">
    <div class="claim"> <div id="CLM-00001" num="00001" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>1</b>. A microporous high density polyethylene film, comprising: 
<div class="claim-text">a composition, comprising: 
<div class="claim-text">20-50 wt % high density polyethylene with a weight average molecular weight of 2×10<sup>5</sup>-5×10<sup>5 </sup>(component I), containing 5 wt % or less molecule with a molecular weight of 1×10<sup>4 </sup>or less; and </div>
<div class="claim-text">80-50 wt % diluent (component II), </div>
</div> <div class="claim-text">wherein, tensile strengths are 1,100 kg/cm<sup>2 </sup>or more in transverse and machine directions respectively, a puncture strength is 0.22 N/μm or more, a gas permeability (Darcy&#39;s permeability constant) is 1.3×10<sup>−5 </sup>Darcy or more, and shrinkages are 5% or less in transverse and machine directions, respectively. </div> </div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00002" num="00002" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>2</b>. The microporous high density polyethylene film as set forth in <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, wherein the component I contains 2 wt % or less comonomer, the comonomer being selected from the group consisting of propylene, butene-1, hexene-1, and 4-methylpentene-1. </div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00003" num="00003" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>3</b>. The microporous high density polyethylene film as set forth in <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, wherein the component II includes a paraffin oil with a kinetic viscosity of 20-200 cSt at 40° C. </div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim"> <div id="CLM-00004" num="00004" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>4</b>. A method of producing a microporous high density polyethylene film, comprising: 
<div class="claim-text">(a) melt-extruding a composition, including 20-50 wt % high density polyethylene with a weight average molecular weight of 2×10<sup>5</sup>-5×10<sup>5 </sup>(component I), containing 5 wt % or less molecule with a molecular weight of 1×10<sup>4 </sup>or less, and 80-50 wt % diluent (component II), to form a sheet; </div> <div class="claim-text">(b) stretching the sheet at a temperature range, where 30-80 wt % of a crystalline portion of the sheet is molten, according to a tenter-type simultaneous stretching manner such that stretching ratios are 3 times or more in machine and transverse directions, respectively and a total stretching ratio is 25-50 times to produce a film; </div> <div class="claim-text">(c) extracting the diluent from the film; and </div> <div class="claim-text">(d) heat-setting the resulting film at a temperature range where 10-30 wt % of a crystalline portion of the film is molten, the microporous high density polyethylene film having tensile strengths of 1,100 kg/cm<sup>2 </sup>or more in transverse and machine directions respectively, a puncture strength of 0.22 N/μm or more, a gas permeability (Darcy&#39;s permeability constant) of 1.3×10<sup>−5 </sup>Darcy or more, and shrinkages of 5% or less in transverse and machine directions, respectively. </div> </div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00005" num="00005" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>5</b>. The method as set forth in <claim-ref idref="CLM-00004">claim 4</claim-ref>, wherein the component I contains 2 wt % or less comonomer, the comonomer being selected from the group consisting of propylene, butene-1, hexene-1, and 4-methylpentene-1. </div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00006" num="00006" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>6</b>. The method as set forth in <claim-ref idref="CLM-00004">claim 4</claim-ref>, wherein the component II includes a paraffin oil with a kinetic viscosity of 20-200 cSt at 40′. </div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00007" num="00007" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>7</b>. The method as set forth in <claim-ref idref="CLM-00004">claim 4</claim-ref>, wherein a content of the diluent remaining in the film is 1 wt % or less in the step of (c). </div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00008" num="00008" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text"> <b>8</b>. The method as set forth in <claim-ref idref="CLM-00004">claim 4</claim-ref>, wherein a heat-setting time is 1-20 min in the step of (d).</div>
    </div>
  </div> </div>
  </div>
  </section>

